## Lore

The Plant-People, called Nurilians or just Plant-People since their own name was forgotten, are an intelligent plant life. On their homeworld they grew rooted in the ground, drew all they needed from soil and sun, and had no predators, which left them helpless when the Splugorth came. The Splugorth saw farmers of unmatched skill in them and spent centuries of Bio-Wizard transmutation teaching them to walk. Millions now tend the fields of Atlantis and every other Splugorth world.

They feel the land and its crops directly, and bring fields to ideal growing conditions. Walking makes them dizzy and their muscles ache in ways they never knew, but the contact with the plants they nurture is enough to keep them going. They do not share an animal''s drives: they live in the moment, enjoy rain, breeze, sun and green fields, and think in terms of life or death, comfort or discomfort. They rarely try to escape, and freed ones seldom join a resistance; the few who help do so because they have nowhere else to go.

## Body

They stand 7 to 8 feet (2.1 to 2.4 m) tall, slimmer than a human, and ancient ones can be twice that size. They weigh 200 to 300 lbs (90 to 135 kg). A transmuted Plant-Person lives about 200 years; a non-mutated one ten times as long.

## GM Notes

Habitat: wherever the Splugorth are; roughly two million are on Rifts Earth, mostly in Atlantis, and only about ten thousand are free. They prefer any climate with plentiful water and sun. Value: unparalleled farmers, sold for an average of 1D6x10,000 credits. Allies: none as such, but they enjoy Druids, the Biomancers of South America, Earth Warlocks, nature spirits and naturalists, and most Shamans honor them as nature spirits. Enemies: only the Splugorth and their Minions; despoilers of nature are viewed with sorrow and disgust.
